{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384850-how-specifically-powerful-are-the-methseulah","id":1384850,"title":"How specifically powerful are the methseulah?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T09:06:26-07:00","id":1384850,"title":"How specifically powerful are the methseulah?","content":"Aka. How powerful are they in plot, not merely stats? Especially in OTHER game lines?<br /> Do you think they\u2019re overpowerful?<br /> <br /> Methseulah are so plot device that some stuff of other game lines also have their traces, which interests me a lot. AFAIK, they\u2019re powerful beyond comprehension:<br /> <br /> 1. Baba Yaga blocked most supernaturals of Russia through Shadow Curtain, garou fear her<br /> <br /> 2. The Sleeping Lord, Maiden of Plague, is beneath the Cairo and makes all supernatural tracks to vampire very difficult, which is even mentioned in Rage Across Egypt <br /> <br /> 3. Mithras, founded the Cult of Mithra, some Celestial Chorus still have faith in it. And he almost wipe out all Bone Chewers and Glass Walkers during his awakening<br /> <br /> 4. The founder of Anda needs some of the most powerful Wan Kuei mystics to destroy him<br /> <br /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-30-2020, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:16:21-07:00","id":1384854,"title":"","content":"Menele and Helen directed their proxies against each other while in torpor, flagrantly breaking rules that apply to younger vampires.<br /> <br /> Menele is something of a walking Chuck Norris joke. He set off the volcano that destroyed Pompeii by frenzying, and later directed the development of the Incan civilization. Critical as I am of V5's use of the Beckoning to clear a lot of elders out of the metaplot, I think might have been warranted in Menele's case. He was ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:23:18-07:00","id":1384856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384850-how-specifically-powerful-are-the-methseulah?p=1384854#post1384854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Menele and Helen directed their proxies against each other while in torpor, flagrantly breaking rules that apply to younger vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also appear in Under a Blood Red Moon<br /> <br /> Menele is described as \u201chave strength no garou can reach\u201d by Uktena. Henela appears in plot and kills several garou with ease","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:46:26-07:00","id":1384860,"title":"","content":"they're as powerful as you want them to be<br /> their only limits are that they can't dominate the 3rd gen and lower, but can be dominated by them<br /> <br /> they are also still cainite, and are still vulnerable to sunlight, have trouble traversing the gauntlet, have a beast etc (something the 3rd gen seem to have less trouble with...I think)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-30-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:57:35-07:00","id":1384862,"title":"","content":"Depend of the edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T10:41:08-07:00","id":1384871,"title":"","content":"I think this boils down to what role you wish them to fill in your story and there are two lines of thought in my mind.<br /> <br /> Unattainable- these creatures are more powerful than the PCs could be and are potentially god like. In this case I don't think they should be given states at all. They are purely a story element to be used at your leisure to move the story as you wish. Deus ex if you will. purely story elements shouldn't have to be stated out.<br /> <br /> Attainable- these are elements in your world that can be defeated and if they can be defeated they should actually be able to be defeated. giving them unattainable stats is, in my mind a waste of time when you are going this route. In this mindset they are something that seem all powerful but in the end are actually not. That doesn't mean they should be defeated easily. they should have stats that bind them to the same rules as the PCs but the PCS now that one day they will be able to become them or overthrow them.<br /> <br /> Novels and other fictional works don't have stats at all for there SPCs and typically use the Unattainable method and only allow the PCs to overcome the Methuslah when it suites the plot of the story being told. in that regard Methuslahs are aways as powerful as the story needs and never follow the rules that other PCs are bound to. If you wish to simulate that in your game then always use the Unattainable method and allow the Methuslah to be defeated when you need them to be. Move them at the speed of plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:23:16-07:00","id":1384907,"title":"","content":"I distinguish between Vampires of a certain age and whether they truly are a Methusaleh in status. Supposedly the change to Methusaleh status (the grave change that moves them from the earthly to the truly supernatural by which point they no longer have any semblance to humanity) is supposed to occur between one thousand and two thousand years of age.<br /> <br /> Yet we have many examples of active vampires of that age who don't seem to be of that status. The game, for example, has lots of Roman era vampires who aren't. But perhaps that is a function of both Generation and Age - if you're 4th or 5th generation, that change occurs between 1000-2000 years, but if you're of higher generation it never happens or takes even more centuries or millennia.<br /> <br /> But even that isn't the whole story. Mithras is older than the Roman Empire and of the 4th generation. Yet he was still active well into the 20th Century. He actually didn't seem to act like a Methusaleh like Baba Yaga or even Menele &amp; Helena (though Menele more than Helena). Neither does Marcus Vitel despite being 2000 years old and of appropriate generation. Same with Inyanga. Louhi, despite being younger than some of these vampires, does seem to be like this.<br /> <br /> So I personally distinguish between these kinds of &quot;Methusalehs&quot;. Mithras, Vitel, and Inyanga don't count even though they should qualify while Baba Yaga, Louhi, an Enkidu do. You can find lots more examples. (Although I would say that it seems Mithras at least was in the process of undergoing the change to true Methusaleh status. It's probable that him going into torpor during the Blitz was not due to a bomb injuring him, but him entering the Sleep of Ages to be transformed into something else. And isn't it a little too convenient that he happened to wake just before he was attacked by a pack of Lupines AND Sabbat at the same time? Sounds more like somehow his resting place became known, and these two separate groups learned about it and attempted to take him out forcing him out of torpor to deal with it. One of those groups likely uncovered the secret, but inadvertently informed the other who went down to spoil it.)<br /> <br /> Since the first kind seem to act like normal vampires, they get treated like them. They're powerful because of their experience and stats, but that's it. They don't get to do strange plot device type antics.<br /> <br /> The second kind who have <i>changed</i> somehow; they get to do the crazy plot device type things. When you get this status, you can become one of the big bads of Vampire or the other game lines.<br /> <br /> It's possible that in order to become the second kind of Methusaleh, you have to undergo some kind of occult ritual or spiritual journey. That would explain why very active vampires don't transition. At some point when you become aware of certain things, you need to start undertaking this quest and prepare yourself for extended voluntarily torpor. That might explain why Mithras disappeared from time to time while he was Prince of London. He was obtaining knowledge and making preparations for the transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:40:44-07:00","id":1384974,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a> <br /> <br /> Keep in mind <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selection_bias\" target=\"_blank\">selection bias</a>. The Methuselahs you mention all have the power to enact big, dramatic magical effects which are felt over an entire region. These are the ancients who get talked about. This can make it seem that all Meths are heavy-hitters.<br /> <br /> There are a vampires who technically satisfy the minimum requirements to count as a Meth (4th or 5th gen, and age 1000yo+), but have a low-key powerset. In <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62250/Elysium-The-Elder-Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Elysium: the Elder Wars</a>, you can build such a creature if you plan your chagen just right. Buying fifth gen is expensive, and Age 5 lowers your starting Humanity, but it's do-able. The starting discipline dots allotment is 10 dots, half of which must be in-clan.<br /> <br /> This power level is not overwhelming.<br /> <br /> You don't hear about them because they understand that powerful blood makes them a target, and they exist quietly in the slow lane. There are probably a good number of low-key meths who just hang out in their havens and pursue their personal hobbies. Some gravitate toward the Inconnu or Autarkis. Some devote themselves to internal clan affairs. Some pretend to be ancilla or low-level elders to keep expectations low.<br /> <br /> Don't agree living low-key is the way to go? How many of the Meths you mention are still around?<br /> <br /> (Just a side note, if you have nine dollars that needs a home, buy Elysium. It is one of the most useful, concise VtM supplements ever. It would be especially helpful for someone who runs games in other lines, but wants crossover vampires. I would even say it should be the second book someone buys, after core.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T11:04:36-07:00","id":1385092,"title":"","content":"Methuselahs are thought of as 4th and 5th gens. But I think there's a big difference between a 4th and a 5th, even if they're both normally too above the average person to consider. A think with vampire ages is that you should account for Torpor and subtract. I'd fear a five hundred year old vampire who's been up every night more than I'd fear someone from the viking age who just came out of a millenia torpor. If a new third gen popped up and didn't have any time to hone their disciplines, they'd be a curiosity before they became lunch.<br /> <br /> It really depends on what disciplines they've been cultivating. Sure, the malkavian might be unseen and near omniscient, but he'd barely be better than your average ancillae in a physical fight.On Vampires that actually cultivate physical disciplines... I'm really not sure. I Tried to houserule new celerity rules that I thought would be reasonable at some point before I realised they completely fall apart when you get to 6+ on an exponential scale. Which, obviously, my houserules aren't canonical, but if you consider that non-physical disciplines seem to have exponentially more powerful powers, Celerity/Potence/Fortitude just giveing an extra dice doesn't seem quite right? Ten fortitude clearly isn't enough to take on a nuke if you take just dice, and Elder physical powers that just 'do' very specific things doesn't seem right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-01-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:33:32-07:00","id":1385118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384850-how-specifically-powerful-are-the-methseulah?p=1385092#post1385092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methuselahs are thought of as 4th and 5th gens. But I think there's a big difference between a 4th and a 5th, even if they're both normally too above the average person to consider..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've noticed that as well. 4th and 5th Gens are both extremely powerful, but 4th gens tend to be more, lets say, 'antediluvian like' and mystical while 5th gens are often more politically involved, and have more presence in night to night affairs. It's the difference betweeen Menele (4th gen) and his childe Critias. Menele is a force of nature, wheras Critias is merely a very powerful elder of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> This can also be seen with Michael/Beshter (4th gen) and his childe, Petronius. Michael himself is only interested in building his holy city into a Cainite utopia, but he has to leave the mundane details of running the city to his 5th gen childe, Petronius, because otherwise things would fall apart.<br /> <br /> So in general, I think that 5th gens are interested in gaining power in a more mortal fashion (political, economical, millitary etc), whilst their 4th gen sires are nearer to the antediluvian sires in that they have very little interest in mundane affairs, and are more focused on esoteric or spiritual goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}